Redhat 7's X does not work.  Here are a few ideas I have found to
be helpful:

  - Try the "--preferxf3" switch in your favorite configuration
    tool, or try a configuration tool that supports that switch.
    At least with my (slow) Permedia2 Oxygen card, this gets my
    system limping at 16-bit color.

  - There are a bunch of Alpha-specific bugs fixed in the latest
    XFree-*-4.02a-1 RPMS, and there is a 4.03-1 set available.

  - I'm told a Nvidia TNT2 card and XFree 4.02 can be made to
    work together, at least on a UP2000.  I'm going to try yet
    again today to see if I can get it to work on my system.

  - If you want to try to debug the XFree 4.0.2 sources, I have
    found that rebuilding from the source RPMs will fail in the
    link step, _unless_ you have installed the 4.0.2 binaries
    _first_.  So, if you install the binaries, then you can
    compile from source, then you can install the binaries you
    built, etc.

If you get RH7 X to work, please post how you did it.

Good luck.

