OK, now for the minor gotcha's for the "a" variant, they could ship with
devices not supported by SRM or XFree86,  your boot message  dk*0.0.0.1009.0
means you probably have an Adaptec controller. The Adaptec is not supported
as a boot device by SRM,  at the SRM prompt do a "show config"

The X problem may mean your system has a TGA card not supported by X,  what
does the init banner say? or the model off the bottom of the panel that the
video connector is on (5d50, 4d30 etc)

It may be easier for you to start with AlphaBios/Milo  then switch to SRM
later, rather than changing the hardware now, but you would still need a
diff video (elsa gloria, or any vga)

RH6.2 is easy to install using alphabios, then upgrade to 7.0.

JJ

