About your X configuration -- Not all video adapters are supported, and it 
can be very difficult to get things working.  

I, personally, think it's too confusing, not educational enough, etc etc, 
and when I need X, I simply buy a known-supported card.  The process 
detects it easily enough, and you don't have to mess with entering manual 
settings.  

If you try the manual way, Here are the possibilites you're facing:

Your card is able to work, you try once or a few times, and get it working.

Your card is able to work, you keep trying and trying, and eventually you 
get it working.

Your card is able to work, you keep trying and trying, and never succeed.

Your card cannot work, but you don't know that, and you keep trying and 
trying, and you were wasting your time right from the start.

The above is not very constructive, I know.  All I am able to say is, good 
luck.  I hope you don't waste much on it.  If I were you, I'd check 
RedHat's list of supported hardware.


