	"G. Hugh Song" <ghsong@nospam.com> writes:

> Between P4 and Athlon, I would choose P4 because of the RAMBUS
> DRAM because many of my codes rely on large matrices which 
> do not fit in any cache structure.  I am sure that most 
> number crunching applications do need such large matrices.

Bear in mind that RDRAM is only fast if accessed sequentially. The high
latency (significantly worse than ordinary SDRAM) makes it slower in many
applications.

And as John says, the P4's FPU is much slower than the P3's, let alone the
Athlon's, so until you get your SSE2 compiler, it looks like being a very
bad choice for numerical work.


