boot drive:

>>> boot dka0 -flags 0
         ^^^^-- or 100 or 200 or ... (drive number * 100 on the adapter,
0==000)
         |||                         (low 2 digits are LUNs (partitions)
in drive)
         ||+--- or b or c or ... (adapter number, see >>> sho dev
output)
         |+---- or r or w or ... (adapter type, k==SCSI )
         +----- or e or r or ... (device type, d==disk, e==ethernet,...)

>>> help boot
will tell more about command options available.

>>> sho config
will show the processor type, memory configuration, bus controllers (if
PCI)

>>> sho dev
will list the available devices, their full address, their type,
firmware
revision, and capacity

