Good question. The multia's SRM does not support IDE drives in the 
sense that it cannot boot from them nor shows them in "show dev" 
(IIRC), but normally you can boot the srm and then boot from scsi or 
network with the IDE drive plugged. I had such a setup here when my 
Multia still lived - I booted a via network, but had the file system 
root on a IDE disk.

Are you sure that you hit the correct IDE connector? I remember some 
confusion about that.

Of course you could try to switch to ARC and see if it supports the 
disk. Maybe you have a broken outdated SRM. But I would not recommend 
updating the SRM unless you definitely find out that the disk works 
with ARC and only does not work with SRM. The reason being that the 
most bugfree SRM versions are not those that you can still download 
from DEC's website. :-|

