processors, as each node in the cluster has the overhead of requiring
a motherboard, RAM, and a hard disk - and physical space that I don't
really have.  On the other hand, CPU price rises superlinearly with
speed.  Looking around, it seems that dual Pentium III/1GHz rackmounted
servers can be had for about =A31600 each; slower machines are not
going to give a better price/performance ratio than this.  Maybe I'll
