Can I put in a recommendation for http://www.sun.com/gridware at this
point.  It has the singular advantage of being free, with the slight
disadvantage that you'll probably need a day buried in the documentation
to get your head around it.

Out experience locally has been that once you get above a very small
number of processors available to you, it becomes massively beneficial
to have some kind of job queue management system available, even if
it's only for one person to use (but even more so if the resource needs
to be shared).

Little things like "run this job only when all these have completed" , and
not having to second guess how long each job will run ... [ nothing more
irritating than sticking twenty jobs (sequentially) on each processor, and 
finding that all the long-running ones are on the same machine ... ]

-patrick.


