You should look over the faqs.

http://www.newfieldinn.com/faq/ 
http://www.alphalinux.org/ 
http://www.tru64.org/ 

There is no such thing as "cmos setup" in alphas, at least not the way 
you're used to if you're coming from x86 background.  The SRM console, 
AlphaBIOS, or ARC console is the interface you use at the lowest level.

There are a few ways you can get there.  

If you can login and get a command prompt in Unix or 
Linux, type 
# shutdown -h now

If you can't do that, when your computer is coming on, 
while you see the ea.e9.e8.e7... messages, 
keep tapping Ctrl-C.

If that doesn't work, try pressing the halt button.  On 
some computers, this is a reset button, so that might not 
work either.  On many, you can configure the halt/reset
button with a jumper.  (The 400 4/233 is one of them, I'm 
pretty sure.)

If all else fails, disconnect your hard drive and turn on 
the computer.  This is guaranteed to stop the regular boot 
process, and you will get a console prompt.  :-)


