Hi all,

I have just completed a port of the satellite tracking routines
in NORAD's Spacetrack report #3, from the original FORTRAN to C.
My port includes all five satellite ephemeris routines (SGP, SGP4,
SDP4, SGP8 and SDP8), a skeleton main() function to demonstrate
the use of these routines and a header file. I have also included
a copy of the original fortran code derived from the pdf version
of the NORAD report and fixed to be acceptable to f2c.

I had to make a lot of changes to the C code to streamline the
structure of the code and to get rid of all the goto's that make
the original source very confusing. This source hacking has likely
resulted in hidden bugs in the final code, as the results produced
by the C routines agree to the 5th or 6th digit with the examples
in NORAD's report.

The C source is in ansi C with no platform-specific calls so it should
work on differnt systems for testing and it should be readily usable
in application code. 

If interested please visit my homepage below to download the package.

