Somebody -- if you know how to disable the local display when you're using 
kdm (i.e. if you only want X through the network) please let me know how.  
Thank you.

With Red Hat 7.0, to make no local X, but allow network X:

using gdm, to enable xdmcp network login:
edit gdm.conf make changes:
	[xdmcp]
	Enable=1

using gdm, to disable local X login:
edit gdm.conf, comment out the line
	[servers]
	#0=blah blah
	#1=blah blah

To switch over, and use KDM instead of GDM:
edit /etc/sysconfig/desktop
    	DESKTOP="KDE1"

using kdm, to enable xdmcp network login:
edit /usr/X11R6/lib/X11/xdm/xdm-config  
    	Go to the end, and comment-out DisplayManager.requestPort 
    	using a ! mark

using kdm, to disable local login:
    	I don't know how.
    	Let me know, please.
    	I find that kdm is more reliable on the network than is gdm.  
    	gdm seems to go down too frequent.


