Dan <s3090872 AT melba DOT vu DOT edu DOT au> wrote:
> Since I can only get my ethernet adapter to run at 100Mb half duplex using
> the de4x5 module, I will need to edit the module so it gets the ethernet
> card to run at 100Mb with full duplex turned on. Obviously the module has
> full duplex turned off by default. Using "insmod de4x5 args='eth0: fdx
> autosense=100Mb' " creates other problems. How do I recompile an edited
> driver module into the kernel on RHL7.0 for Alpha?

Things aren't much different betweeh x86 and Alpha, except
possibly the actual safe install of a new kernel.

cd /usr/src/linux
more README

cd path/to/whatever/source
  edit source
cd /usr/src/linux

Next, do you want it to be a module (generally recommended), 
or in the kernel. In general 

make mrproper
make menuconfig
  find Network device support, choose the card
  if kernel
    make sure it's marked as *
  else
    make sure it's marked as M
  fi
make dep
if kernel
  make
fi
make modules
make modules_install

Then if you've compiled a new kernel install it, I think how to do
that varies slightly depending on whether you're using SRM or MILO.
I've not got round to a kernel recompile on RH7Alpha yet... Just make
sure that however you do it that you can boot to the old kernel
just in case something goes wrong.

