My notes say to do a `make boot' after the make dep, which leaves
a compressed kernel in arch/alpha/boot/vmlinux.gz --as you say.
You got your kernel, so the `make modules' must have built it
through a dependency.  I copy the compressed kernel manually to my
boot partition, giving it a unique name like vmlinux-m.n.p.gz to
avoid clobbering older kernels.  I always boot manually from milo,
e.g.

    MILO> boot sdb1:vmlinux-m.n.p.gz root=/dev/sda3

The System.map has to do with modules and goes in /usr/src/linux .
If I remember correctly, failing to update it causes warnings during boot,
but the kernel still works.

