Artem Kazantsev wrote:
>> >
>> > Hey,
>> > Did anyone here successfully  install RH7 on PC164UX or BX ?

Yes, I did (technically one of betas for RH7 and not a release as later
I did not have this machine anymore).  On UX. No problems save one - due
to an error in startup files which forces '-A' to 'hwclock' when nobody
asked for that you are coming with a clock shifted down by 20 years;
easy to correct.

>>
>> Seems it can't find the root-partition. I think it has to be
>> something
>> like:
>> MILO> boot -t iso9660 hda:/kernels/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/hdaX
>> where X is youre root-partition.
>>

> No, I tried root=/dev/hda and root=/dev/hda1 - does not work.

Eh? Why it should?  /dev/hda is your CD so there is nothing on /dev/hda1
and indeed there is no 'init' which you could use on /dev/hda.  It wants
a root on ramdisk but your milo is not likely to support initrd.  Typing
random stuff is not a replacement for understanding.

Do that instead.  Make a ramdisk on a floppy by dumping
images/ramdisk.img to it ('cat ramdisk.img > /dev/fd0', or
'dd if=ramdisk.img of=/dev/fd0 size=1440k', or 'rawrite.exe', or any of
equivalents).  Put both CD and a floppy in their drives and, at Milo
prompt, type

  boot hda:kernels/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

Hit <Return> when asked for a floppy.  Continue with an installation.

  Michal


